Title: error handling for keeping status errors over transport errors

This is the first of multiple PRs for handling https://github.com/grafana/pir-actions/issues/595.

In this PR `StatusErrorFromResponse` is added to support converting grpc based errors to status errors, including transport errors. Currently transport errors are passed through when using `ErrorFromResponse` which has side effects like a `500` being reported although the attached `ErrorResult` would be a `4xx`. 

Follow up PRs will handle how error handling is done in consumers, e.g. 

change from 
```go
	resp, err := h.clientFor(primary).Search(ctx, searchReq)
	if err != nil {
		return nil, "", err
	}
	if resp.Error != nil {
		return nil, "", resource.GetError(resp.Error)
	}
``` 
to
```go
resp, err := h.clientFor(primary).Search(ctx, searchReq)
if err := resource.StatusErrorFromResponse(resp.GetError(), err); err != nil {
	return nil, "", err
}
```

This PR includes a change in `errhttp.Write` (`pkg/util`) which is used in many different places and owned by @grafana/grafana-backend-services-squad

